From e073fb0a2484de19087e9baf74e1b6b137a839f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pablo Lopez <plopez@unc.edu.ar>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:07:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add magnetic field fields (B, grad B, div B, curl B) for
 SWIFT snapshots

New '--field' choices: magnetic, magneticGradient, magneticDivergence,
magneticCurl and their averaged '_a' versions, written to .mag, .magGrad,
.magDiv, .magCurl (.a_*). They can be computed in the same run as the
density and velocity fields.

- The HDF5 reader (--input 105) reads /PartType0/MagneticFluxDensities
  when a magnetic field is requested; only gas particles can be selected.
- B is interpolated as the 3 components of the scalar data (NO_SCALARS=3
  in the Makefile); div B and curl B are computed from its gradient on
  the full grid (like the velocity divergence and vorticity).
- Consistency checks: 3D, NO_SCALARS=3, DTFE method, HDF5 input, gas only,
  not combined with the 'scalar' fields or the gas temperature.
- README: magnetic fields section and a note on the Monte Carlo noise of
  the averaged fields.

Tested with B=(x+y,-x+y+z,2x+z) and v=(2x,-y,3z) in one run: B, grad B,
div B=3, curl B=(-1,-2,-2), v, div v=4 and vort v=0 are reproduced to
1e-5 at the grid points; identical results with one/two files, periodic
box, --partition and several threads. Gadget results are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C44ZCErHKsQgk681XW3FMn
